kokkos-kernels
------------------------------------------
KokkosKernels implements local computational kernels for linear algebra and
graph operations, using the Kokkos shared-memory parallel programming model.
'Local' means not using MPI, or running within a single MPI process without
knowing about MPI. 'Computational kernels' are coarse-grained operations; they
take a lot of work and make sense to parallelize inside using Kokkos.
KokkosKernels can be the building block of a parallel linear algebra library
like Tpetra that uses MPI and threads for parallelism, or it can be used
stand-alone in your application.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libkokkos5.3-5.3.0-1bl1
  libkokkoskernels-devel-5.3.0-1bl1
  libkokkoskernels5.3-5.3.0-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libkokkos-devel-5.3.0-1bl1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/kokkos/kokkos-kernels

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/kokkos/kokkos-kernels/archive/refs/tags/5.3.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack kokkos-kernels-5.3.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./kokkos-kernels-5.3.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/kokkos-kernels-5.3.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/kokkos-kernels-5.3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libkokkoskernels5.3-5.3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libkokkoskernels-devel-5.3.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

